  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of the EU Exploratory Mission (ExM) to DR Congo 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The European Union will send an election exploratory mission to DRC to assess the usefulness, advisability and feasibility of a fully-fledged EU Election Observation Mission for the upcoming presidential, legislative, provincial and local elections in DRC (schedule for 20 December 2023). IOM will identify seven experts (one electoral/political expert, one legal expert, one media expert, one logistics expert and a deputy, one security expert and a deputy), who will travel to Kinshasa for approximately 15 days, to collect factual information on the election process, make necessary preliminary logistics enquiries and provide advice on how to organize the operational component of a possible EU EOM and assess the security situation in the country.IOM will have no visibility and will not be associated to the work or the reports written by the experts; IOM will provide administrative, logistics and security support to the ExM.</narrative>
  </description>
